822 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Having read through both flowcharts closely\054 here\047s my honest read\056\n\nThe two diagrams aren\047t really describing different products \024 they\047re describing different stories about the same product\056 In both versions\054 the same ten\055ish capabilities exist\054 and your own board betrays how interconnected they are\072 the AI Assistant calls Drafting and Translator as tools\054 Case Management feeds Legal Research\054 Document Scanner outputs get assigned to case files\054 OCR exists specifically to serve eFiling\056 Architecturally\054 you\047ve built a platform\056 The question is purely how you want the world to enter it\056\n\nThe platform framing is the stronger long\055term story\056 \042Lexli is the workspace for an advocate\042 \050your own words on the board\051 is a clear\054 ownable position \024 it says the whole is worth more than the parts\054 it justifies a subscription rather than \340\055la\055carte pricing\054 and it makes every new tool you ship feel like the platform getting more valuable rather than a new thing to market\056 Its weakness is acquisition\072 nobody searches Google for \042legal workspace\056\042 They search \042translate judgment to Marathi\054\042 \042check case status by CNR\054\042 \042cause list for tomorrow\056\042 A monolithic platform pitch asks a busy advocate to buy a whole new way of working before they\047ve gotten any value from you\056\nThe products framing is the mirror image\056 Each tool becomes a doorway \024 its own landing page\054 its own search intent\054 its own \042try it free in 30 seconds\042 moment\056 That\047s excellent for a starter\055stage company that needs top\055of\055funnel\056 But as the primary identity\054 \042a series of products\042 is a weaker position\072 it fragments a small team\047s marketing effort across ten product identities\054 it invites feature\055by\055feature comparison with point solutions \050every OCR tool\054 every translation tool\051\054 and it undersells your actual advantage\054 which is that these tools share cases\054 files\054 and context\056 A bundle is easy to unbundle\073 a workspace isn\047t\056\n\nThere\047s also a signal in your own homepage ideation that I think resolves this\072 the three doorways \024 Advocates\054 Law Firms \046 Businesses\054 Citizens\056 Advocates and firms want the platform story\073 they live in this world daily and the integrated workspace is the sell\056 Citizens will almost never want a platform \024 they want to check one case\054 translate one document\056 So your audiences themselves split across the two framings\056\n\nWhich is why I\047d land on\072 one brand\054 platform\055first identity\054 products as entry points\056 Portray Lexli AI as the legal platform \024 that\047s the headline\054 the vision\054 the thing investors and firms buy\056 Then let the individual tools exist as named\054 individually discoverable features of the platform \050with their own pages and possibly free standalone use for citizen\055grade tasks like Case Finder or Translator\051\054 each funneling into the full workspace\056 That\047s essentially what your second diagram is reaching for\054 but I\047d change one thing about it\072 don\047t present Platform and Products as siblings under Lexli AI\054 because that implies two separate businesses and will confuse pricing\054 navigation\054 and messaging\056 The products live inside the platform\073 some of them just have their own front doors\056\n\nPractically\054 that means the website says \042Lexli \024 the AI platform for Indian legal practice\042 at the top\054 the nav has a Platform story page and a Tools dropdown\054 and each tool page ends in the same place\072 the platform\056 If it would help\054 I can sketch this as a third flowchart on the board \024 the hybrid IA \024 or map it into a concrete sitemap for the website\056 Also worth noting Figma has me on a View seat\054 so to draw into the board itself you\047d need to bump that to an edit seat\073 otherwise I can deliver it as a diagram file here\056)
     /K [ 152 ]
     /P 823 0 R
     /Pg 518 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

